WEBVTT

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.020
<v Ira Glass>From WBEZ Chicago, it's This American Life. I'm Ira Glass.
<v Ira Glass>这里是芝加哥WBEZ电台，《美国生活》节目。我是艾拉·格拉斯。

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.890
<v Ira Glass>OK. So we're going through the gate here into the park?
<v Ira Glass>好的。那我们现在正穿过大门进入公园吗？

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:17.160
<v Cole Lindbergh>Yeah, we're going-- this is our morning-- this is the morning walk into the park. See, everybody will split up into their different sections and get the park open. And we'll start putting out prizes and--
<v Cole Lindbergh>是的，我们正要去——这是我们的早晨——这是进入公园的晨间漫步。看，每个人都会分散到各自的区域，准备开园。我们一会儿就开始摆放奖品，然后……

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:43.990
<v Ira Glass>We're at an amusement park in Kansas City, Missouri called Worlds of Fun. We're going to be spending the entire hour today at amusement parks. It's five minutes before opening, and I'm walking with Cole Lindbergh, who's 25 with permanently-mussed hair and the cheerful vibe of the Bosom Buddies-era Tom Hanks. He's been coming to this park since he was a little kid, started working here as a summer job at 14, and then basically just never left. It became his real job. 11 years later, he is a full-time, year-round employee.
<v Ira Glass>我们现在在密苏里州堪萨斯城的“欢乐世界”游乐园。今天整个小时我们都将在游乐园度过。距离开园还有五分钟，我正和25岁的科尔·林德伯格同行，他头发总是乱糟糟的，有着《肥佬教授》时代汤姆·汉克斯那种开朗的气质。他从小就来这个公园玩，14岁时在这里做暑期工，之后基本上就没离开过。这份工作成了他的正职。11年后，他成了一名全职的全年雇员。

00:00:43.990 --> 00:01:00.460
<v Cole Lindbergh>I love amusement parks. Any time my family would go on vacation, we'd schedule it around an amusement park, because I love roller coasters. I loved amusement parks. I mean, I've walked-- this pathway that we're taking right now-- I've walked it thousands and thousands and thousands of times.
<v Cole Lindbergh>我爱游乐园。每当家人去度假，我们总会把游乐园排进日程，因为我喜欢过山车。我热爱游乐园。我的意思是，我走过——我们现在走的这条路——我走过成千上万次了。

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:24.800
<v Ira Glass>When he was little, his family had season passes here, and they would come a lot. He'd travel to any new roller coaster to try it out, daydreamed about a job where he would design parks and build roller coasters. And when his dad drove him here at the age of 14 for a job interview-- he wore a suit to that interview-- just sitting inside the park's offices, which are utilitarian-- picture the principal's office at a public high school-- even that was exciting.
<v Ira Glass>他小时候，家里有这里的季票，他们常来。他会去尝试任何新的过山车，梦想着有一份设计公园和建造过山车的工作。当他14岁时父亲开车送他来面试——他穿了西装——坐在公园办公室里，那里很简朴——想象一下公立高中的校长办公室——即使那样也让他感到兴奋。

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:55.260
<v Cole Lindbergh>I remember being like, oh, wow. This is the inner sanctum. This is the inner workings. This is where all the cool stuff happens. And then the first time actually getting in the uniform, actually working at the park-- I remember, to me, it was like, wow. This is surreal. I'm actually working in an amusement park now. And to me, that was kind of, like, awesome. That was awesome. I'm so excited about this.
<v Cole Lindbergh>我记得当时心想，哇。这是核心区域。这是内部运作机制。这就是酷事发生的地方。然后第一次穿上制服，真正开始在公园工作时——我记得，对我来说，就像，哇。这太超现实了。我竟然真的在游乐园工作了。对我来说，那感觉真是太棒了。太棒了。我对此感到非常兴奋。

00:01:55.260 --> 00:02:18.920
<v Ira Glass>You might think that enthusiasm would diminish over time. But what's incredible about Cole is that, even after a decade here, even after becoming an adult and working 60-, 70-hour weeks, every week, all summer, even with the pressure in his current job of running a whole department and hitting financial targets and buying all the supplies and hiring and supervising over 100 young people, he is still pretty psyched about working at an amusement park.
<v Ira Glass>你可能认为这种热情会随着时间推移而消退。但科尔不可思议的地方在于，即使在这里待了十年，即使已经成年并每周工作60到70个小时，整个夏天都如此，即使还要承受目前管理整个部门、达到财务目标、采购所有用品、雇用并监管100多名年轻人的压力，他依然对在游乐园工作感到非常兴奋。

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:36.770
<v Ira Glass>And it is not a glamour job. The department Cole runs is the games department at Worlds of Fun. This is 32 games, the kind that you would see at any carnival or midway, where you get three softballs to try to throw them into a milk can, or you throw beanbags at targets, or you shoot darts to knock over a stack of cups.
<v Ira Glass>但这并不是一份光鲜的工作。科尔管理的部门是“欢乐世界”的游艺项目部。这里有32个游戏，就是你在任何嘉年华或游乐场都能看到的那些，比如给你三个垒球尝试投进奶罐，或者向目标投掷豆袋，又或者是扔飞镖击倒一堆杯子。

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:52.790
<v Ira Glass>Nobody comes to an amusement park for the games. Cole himself never went to an amusement park for the games. But he's an extrovert, and he has filled the department with extroverts, like Mallory. The park is barely open-- hardly any customers here at all-- when Cole stops by her game on his morning rounds.
<v Ira Glass>没人是为了玩游戏才来游乐园的。科尔本人以前来游乐园也不是为了玩这些游戏。但他是个外向的人，他也为部门招募了像马洛里这样外向的员工。公园刚开门——几乎没什么游客——科尔在晨间巡视时顺便去了她的摊位。

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:55.700
<v Cole Lindbergh>Yeah, Mallory loves talking on the mic. Mallory does a good job on the mic.
<v Cole Lindbergh>是啊，马洛里很喜欢用麦克风说话。马洛里用麦克风的表现很不错。

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.570
<v Mallory>(WHISPERING) Thank you! I appreciate it.
<v Mallory>（耳语）谢谢！我很感激。

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:02.120
<v Cole Lindbergh>Let's hear it. Go for it. Try to get people to play.
<v Cole Lindbergh>让我们听听看。开始吧。试着拉人来玩。

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:17.050
<v Mallory>All righty. We're over here at three-point challenge today looking for out first winner! You come on over here. You have 40 seconds on the clock, 12 shots up, and you could be walking away with some awesome prizes! We have--
<v Mallory>好的。我们今天在“三分投篮挑战”这里寻找第一位赢家！快过来。你有40秒时间，投12球，你就有机会赢走超级棒的奖品！我们有……

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:36.370
<v Ira Glass>This is exactly how Cole trains the kids to talk on the mic. Don't stop. Get a flow. Have fun. If you have fun, that's what's going to sell the game. Watching Cole run the games department at Worlds of Fun is watching somebody who was raised here and who completely, thoroughly mastered everything. It's rare to witness somebody so happily great at any job.
<v Ira Glass>这就是科尔如何训练孩子们使用麦克风的。不要停。保持节奏。玩得开心。如果你玩得开心，那就能卖出游戏。看科尔管理“欢乐世界”的游艺部门，就像看着一个在这里长大并完全、彻底掌握了一切的人。能看到有人如此快乐且出色地完成工作，这很罕见。

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:41.290
<v Cole Lindbergh>All right. Let's gather around, guys. Is there still people in cash patrol? Anybody know?
<v Cole Lindbergh>好了。大家聚过来。还有人在“现金巡逻队”吗？有人知道吗？

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:47.380
<v Ira Glass>It's the first shift meeting of the day. About 30 teenagers and college kids mill around a big tree before their shifts start.
<v Ira Glass>这是当天第一次轮班会议。大约30名青少年和大学生在轮班开始前围着一棵大树聚集。

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:57.910
<v Cole Lindbergh>All right, guys. Listen up. Gather round. Let's do this. Here we go. Shh. Quiet, please. Real quick. Real quick. Here we go. Today is Saturday.
<v Cole Lindbergh>好了，伙计们。听着。围过来。我们开始吧。来吧。嘘。安静点，请。快点。快点。我们开始吧。今天是星期六。

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:58.690
<v Man>Oh, yeah!
<v Man>哦，耶！

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:17.800
<v Cole Lindbergh>Today is a busy day. Today is the day that we have a very good day, because there are going to be a lot of people playing games. And today, of course, is one of my favorite days of the season. It is the second round of the Sweet 16 Tournament. Let's take a look. Sam, do you want to hold this up a little higher? OK. We've got--
<v Cole Lindbergh>今天是个忙碌的日子。今天注定会是很棒的一天，因为会有很多人来玩游戏。当然，今天也是我本赛季最喜欢的日子之一。今天是“甜蜜16强”锦标赛的第二轮。我们来看看。萨姆，你能把这个举高一点吗？好。我们有……

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:37.930
<v Ira Glass>One of the guys, Sam, holds up a poster board with tournament brackets on it, like for any sports tournament. The Sweet 16 Tournament pits the kids in all 32 games in the park against each other, in pairs, in a four-week competition to make the most money. Last week, half the games were eliminated. Cole is here letting the remaining games know who they're competing with today.
<v Ira Glass>其中一个伙计萨姆举起一张带有锦标赛对阵表的宣传板，就像任何体育赛事那样。“甜蜜16强”锦标赛让公园里所有32个游戏的员工两两配对，在为期四周的比赛中争夺最高营收。上周，一半的游戏被淘汰了。科尔在这里通知剩余的游戏组今天他们的对手是谁。

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:57.770
<v Cole Lindbergh>We have Pigs of Fury, Bullpen versus Goblet Toss, Lion's Den. Now-- can you hold that for me real quick? Now-- wait, hold on! Before we go any further, could this possibly be a precursor for today? Yesterday, the number-one game in the park was Scale Africa.
<v Cole Lindbergh>我们有“愤怒之猪”、“牛棚”对阵“高脚杯投掷”、“狮穴”。现在——你能帮我拿一下这个吗？现在——等等，等一下！在我们继续之前，这会不会是今天的预兆？昨天，公园里排名第一的游戏是“非洲秤重”。

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:00.220
<v Cole Lindbergh>[CHEERING]
<v Cole Lindbergh>（欢呼）

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:28.620
<v Ira Glass>OK. Scale Africa is a scale-- a game where they guess your weight or age. And it's in the Africa part of the park, hence Scale Africa. And it's no surprise that it's number one. It always makes tons of money. All the games in the park are grouped together into four different teams, which they call Games I, Games II, Games III, and Games IV. And these four teams-- Games I through IV-- compete against each other all summer long, like teams at summer camp, in a three-month-long color war.
<v Ira Glass>好。“非洲秤重”是一个秤——一个猜测你体重或年龄的游戏。它在公园的非洲区，所以叫“非洲秤重”。它排名第一并不奇怪。它总是能赚很多钱。公园里所有的游戏被分成四个不同的组，他们称之为游戏I、游戏II、游戏III和游戏IV。这四个组——游戏I到IV——整个夏天都在相互竞争，就像夏令营的队伍，进行为期三个月的颜色大战。

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:44.940
<v Ira Glass>Most other amusement parks don't go this far to make things interesting for the workers. This park, Worlds of Fun, is owned by a company called Cedar Fair that owns 11 amusement parks and six water parks. And Cole knows the guys who run the games departments at the other parks. And some of them do competitions like this between the employees.
<v Ira Glass>大多数其他游乐园不会为了让员工觉得有趣而做到这一步。这个“欢乐世界”公园由雪松会公司拥有，该公司拥有11个游乐园和6个水上乐园。科尔认识其他公园游艺部门的管理人员。他们中的一些人也确实在员工之间搞过这种竞赛。

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:55.070
<v Cole Lindbergh>But I don't think they do it to the extent of what we do. Yeah, we-- every year, I talk about-- we had the Death Match Tournament. We have the Sweet 16 Tournament.
<v Cole Lindbergh>但我觉得他们没做到我们这种程度。是的，我们……每年，我说的是……我们有“死斗锦标赛”。我们有“甜蜜16强”锦标赛。

00:05:55.070 --> 00:06:20.640
<v Cole Lindbergh>A couple years ago, we did a thing called Toss the Boss. And basically what happened was is that, every single day, I'd pull a game out of the hat. And if that game was the number-one game in the park for that day, then that section would get to throw me in the pond. The pond is not a good-looking pond. It's gross, and it smells. And the deal was is that, if you are the number-one game in the park, you get to throw me in the pond.
<v Cole Lindbergh>几年前，我们搞了一个叫“扔老板”的活动。基本上就是，每天我会从帽子里抽出一个游戏。如果那个游戏当天是公园里的第一名，那么那一组就可以把我扔进池塘。那个池塘看起来不怎么样。它很恶心，还有臭味。规矩就是，如果你是公园第一名的游戏，你就可以把我扔进池塘。

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:27.240
<v Ira Glass>So finally, one day, the game that he picked from the hat that day tried their hardest and actually became the number-one game in the park for the day. And--
<v Ira Glass>终于有一天，他从帽子里抽出的那组游戏拼尽全力，真的成为了当天公园里的第一名。然后……

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:28.190
<v Man>Ready?
<v Man>准备好了吗？

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:32.960
<v Crowd>1, 2, 3!
<v Crowd>1，2，3！

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:33.920
<v Crowd>[SPLASH]
<v Crowd>（水花声）

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:34.870
<v Crowd>[CHEERING]
<v Crowd>（欢呼）

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.750
<v Cole Lindbergh>D'oh!
<v Cole Lindbergh>哎呀！

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:48.160
<v Ira Glass>Of course, they made a video about this because it's present-day America. And Cole went and told his peers, his colleagues-- the guys who run the games departments at the other parks-- all about what happened.
<v Ira Glass>当然，他们拍了视频，因为这就是当今的美国。科尔把发生的事告诉了他的同行，他的同事们——那些在其他公园管理游艺部门的人。

00:06:48.160 --> 00:07:17.890
<v Cole Lindbergh>I go and I tell the other parks about this. And I showed a picture. Like, oh, there's me all soaking wet. And I got laughed at. Like, why would you ever do that? And to me, in my mind, I was just like, why would you not do that? Why would you not want to get people excited about working in the game that they're in? At least they may try. They may do a little bit more. And if I can get a little bit more out of them, we're good, even if the game only makes a little bit more money.
<v Cole Lindbergh>我去告诉其他公园这件事。我还展示了照片。就像，哦，看我全身湿透的样子。结果我被嘲笑了。他们问，你为什么要那样做？而在我心里，我只是觉得，为什么不呢？为什么不想让大家对自己负责的游戏感到兴奋呢？至少他们可能会去尝试。他们可能会多做一点。如果我能从他们身上多榨出一点点，我们就赚到了，哪怕那个游戏只多赚了一点钱。

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:19.330
<v Ira Glass>Also, it's more fun for the kids.
<v Ira Glass>而且，这对孩子们来说也更有趣。

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.180
<v Cole Lindbergh>Exactly. It's all about more fun.
<v Cole Lindbergh>没错。一切都是为了更有趣。

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:30.190
<v Cole Lindbergh>All right. So there's a lot of people in the park today. Now, I have composed a song about today, which I now want to sing for you.
<v Cole Lindbergh>好了。今天公园里人很多。现在，我写了一首关于今天的歌，我打算现在唱给你们听。

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:30.740
<v Man>Everybody close--
<v Man>大家靠近……

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:45.220
<v Cole Lindbergh>And you can all sing along. [STRUMS GUITAR] OK. (SINGING) Saturday. It's Saturday, Saturday, Saturday, Saturday.
<v Cole Lindbergh>你们都可以跟着唱。（弹吉他）好。（歌唱）星期六。今天是星期六，星期六，星期六，星期六。

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:46.620
<v Man>So wait, what day is it? I forgot.
<v Man>等等，今天是星期几？我忘了。

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.140
<v Cole Lindbergh>It's Saturday.
<v Cole Lindbergh>是星期六。

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:50.370
<v Man>Oh, OK.
<v Man>哦，好的。

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:55.100
<v Cole Lindbergh>(SINGING) Today, I don't feel like riding any rides.
<v Cole Lindbergh>（歌唱）今天，我不想去坐任何游乐设施。

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:55.810
<v Man>Whistle, whistle.
<v Man>口哨，口哨。

00:07:55.810 --> 00:08:11.580
<v Cole Lindbergh>(SINGING) I just want to play all the games. And I really like playing Mamba Ball-- win a giant top frog or a big basketball. Yes, today, I don't feel like riding any rides, just playing games.
<v Cole Lindbergh>（歌唱）我只想玩所有的游戏。我真的很喜欢玩曼巴球——赢一只巨大的青蛙或一个大篮球。是的，今天，我不想坐游乐设施，只想玩游戏。

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.140
<v Crowd>(SINGING) Whoo-hoo! Whoo! Whoo-hoo, hoo, hoo, hoo, hoo, hoo!
<v Crowd>（歌唱）喔呜！喔！喔呜，呜，呜，呜，呜，呜！

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.430
<v Cole Lindbergh>All right. Let's have a good day, guys. Everybody in, all right?
<v Cole Lindbergh>好了。祝大家今天过得愉快，伙计们。所有人，准备好了吗？

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.420
<v Cole Lindbergh>[CHEERING]
<v Cole Lindbergh>（欢呼）

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:20.610
<v Cole Lindbergh>All right. Games on three! 1, 2, 3!
<v Cole Lindbergh>好。数到三就喊“游戏”！1，2，3！

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:21.370
<v Crowd>Games!
<v Crowd>游戏！

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:22.420
<v Cole Lindbergh>All right. Let's have a good day.
<v Cole Lindbergh>好。祝大家度过愉快的一天。

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:42.020
<v Ira Glass>Well, today, on our radio show, we go to amusement parks all over the country. We see stuff backstage that we had no idea was going on, like that song. We hear Jonathan Goldstein's story about moving to the Jersey Shore for a summer when he was 16, and we hear your stories. We asked you to call in with your amusement park stories, and you told some great ones.
<v Ira Glass>今天在我们的广播节目中，我们将前往全国各地的游乐园。我们看到了我们完全不知道发生的幕后事情，比如那首歌。我们将听到乔纳森·戈尔茨坦关于16岁那年搬到新泽西海岸度过一个夏天的故事，也会听到你们的故事。我们曾邀请你们打来电话分享你们的游乐园故事，你们讲了一些非常棒的故事。

00:08:42.020 --> 00:09:13.010
<v Ira Glass>Today's show was recorded and first broadcast a few years ago when you could attend amusement parks without wearing a face mask or taking precautions to avoid a deadly and deeply-contagious coronavirus. Let us return to those happy days, shall we? It's summer. It's hot. Let's spend an hour at a really fun place at a safe social distance-- in fact, the safest imaginable-- that is, over the radio. Let's ride the rides. Let's gorge out on terrible great food together for an hour. Cue the roller coaster sound now!
<v Ira Glass>今天的节目是在几年前录制并首次播出的，那时候你们可以去游乐园而无需戴口罩或采取预防措施来避免致命且具有高度传染性的冠状病毒。让我们回到那些快乐的日子，好吗？夏天到了。天气很热。让我们在一个非常有趣的地方花一个小时，保持安全的社交距离——事实上，是能想象到的最安全的方式——那就是，通过无线电。让我们去坐游乐设施吧。让我们一起花一个小时大吃特吃那些糟糕但美味的食物。现在播放过山车的声音！

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:15.940
<v Ira Glass>[ROLLER COASTER SOUND]
<v Ira Glass>（过山车声音）

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:28.630
<v Ira Glass>Stay with us.
<v Ira Glass>留下来陪我们。

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:45.240
<v Ira Glass>Act One. Gameboy Grows Up. Following Cole Lindbergh around on his early-morning tour of Words of Fun park, I learned a couple things. First of all, people play the games because they want to win the prizes. And so an important part of his job is actually guessing what prizes are going to excite people.
<v Ira Glass>第一幕。游戏男孩长大了。跟随着科尔·林德伯格参观“欢乐世界”公园的清晨之旅，我学到了几件事。首先，人们玩游戏是因为他们想赢奖品。所以他工作的一个重要部分其实是猜测什么样的奖品会让人兴奋。

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:50.250
<v Cole Lindbergh>We kind of just go, it is what it is. Oh, I've got to show you the lemur. Do you want to see what a lemur is?
<v Cole Lindbergh>我们基本上就是，顺其自然。哦，我得让你看看狐猴。你想看看狐猴是什么吗？

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:50.580
<v Ira Glass>Yeah.
<v Ira Glass>好啊。

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:56.250
<v Cole Lindbergh>People love these. This is a lemur. People play for this all the time. This is one of our number-one prizes.
<v Cole Lindbergh>人们喜欢这些。这就是狐猴。人们总是为了这个玩游戏。这是我们排名第一的奖品之一。

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:56.880
<v Ira Glass>Really?
<v Ira Glass>真的吗？

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:57.800
<v Cole Lindbergh>Yeah.
<v Cole Lindbergh>是啊。

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:14.190
<v Ira Glass>Who'd have thought? It's a fluorescent-colored monkey, the size of a teddy bear, with huge eyes and a super-long tail. When they put it into the dart game, the dart game became one of the most popular games in the park-- doubled its business. I also learned that Cole invents games.
<v Ira Glass>谁能想到呢？这是一只荧光色的猴子，有泰迪熊那么大，眼睛很大，还有一条超长的尾巴。当他们把它放进飞镖游戏时，飞镖游戏成了公园里最受欢迎的游戏之一——生意翻了一倍。我还了解到科尔会发明游戏。

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.230
<v Cole Lindbergh>You like Angry Birds, right?
<v Cole Lindbergh>你喜欢《愤怒的小鸟》，对吧？

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:18.840
<v Ira Glass>We round a corner and I see why he asked.
<v Ira Glass>我们绕过拐角，我明白了为什么他会这么问。

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:31.950
<v Cole Lindbergh>What we're looking at right now is a giant slingshot with a launcher that you launch, basically, beanbags at pigs. And we built this.
<v Cole Lindbergh>我们现在看到的是一个巨大的弹弓发射器，你基本上是用它发射豆袋去打猪。这个是我们自己造的。

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:34.440
<v Ira Glass>So you got permission from the Angry Birds people--
<v Ira Glass>所以你得到了《愤怒的小鸟》版权方的许可……

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.700
<v Cole Lindbergh>Well--
<v Cole Lindbergh>嗯……

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:43.770
<v Ira Glass>This turns out to be an awkward question. Cole points out that this slingshot game is not actually called Angry Birds.
<v Ira Glass>这成了一个尴尬的问题。科尔指出，这个弹弓游戏其实并不叫《愤怒的小鸟》。

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:52.100
<v Cole Lindbergh>It's called Pigs of Fury-- Pigs of Fury. So now this is one of our number-one games. People love shooting a giant slingshot.
<v Cole Lindbergh>它叫“愤怒之猪”——“愤怒之猪”。所以现在这是我们排名第一的游戏。人们喜欢用巨大的弹弓射击。

00:10:52.100 --> 00:11:12.840
<v Ira Glass>Before I flew out to Kansas City to meet Cole, I watched his YouTube videos online. Yes, he has YouTube videos, and I heartily recommend them. They are shot, directed, and starring Cole. They are low-tech. They're low-budget. In this one, he wears a Viking helmet, and a fake mustache, and wire-rimmed glasses. And he's walking through a video arcade. Those are his echoey footsteps that you're hearing.
<v Ira Glass>在我飞往堪萨斯城见科尔之前，我上网看了他的YouTube视频。是的，他有YouTube视频，我强烈推荐它们。它们由科尔拍摄、导演并主演。它们低科技、低预算。在这个视频里，他戴着维京头盔、假胡子和铁丝框眼镜。他正走过一个游戏厅。你听到的就是他那回响的脚步声。

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:27.490
<v Ira Glass>Next, he's inside what looks like-- you know those old arcade machines with the mechanical claw that picks up prizes? This one is big enough for a person to stand inside, and Cole is inside it, surrounded by huge stuffed animals. And he raps.
<v Ira Glass>接下来，他在一个看起来像……你知道那种带机械爪抓奖品的老式游戏机吗？这一个大到可以容纳一个人站在里面，科尔就在里面，周围堆满了巨大的毛绒动物。然后他开始饶舌。

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:38.420
<v Cole Lindbergh>(RAPPING) I give out prizes when you come play my games. If you see me with a mic, I guess it's your birthday. I'm a really cool guy because I make winners every day. Win a bear, a dog, and a giant mon-kay.
<v Cole Lindbergh>（饶舌）当你来玩我的游戏时，我就送出奖品。如果你看到我拿着麦克风，我想那是你的生日。我真是个酷家伙，因为我每天都在制造赢家。赢一只熊，一只狗，还有一只巨大的猴子。

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:48.760
<v Ira Glass>OK, I'm going to stop the video right there. When he says "a bear, a dog, and a giant mon-kay," then we have three quick shots of stuffed animal prizes-- a bear, a dog, and a giant mon-kay.
<v Ira Glass>好了，视频就停在这儿。当他说“一只熊，一只狗，还有一只巨大的猴子”时，我们会有三个毛绒奖品的快速镜头——一只熊，一只狗，还有一只巨大的猴子。

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:54.390
<v Cole Lindbergh>(RAPPING) Sometimes people just don't play games. I'm asking how they're doing, and they say, "No way!"
<v Cole Lindbergh>（饶舌）有时人们就是不玩游戏。我问他们怎么样，他们说，“没门！”

00:11:54.390 --> 00:12:16.790
<v Ira Glass>As the video continues, the teenagers on his staff join him. And they're all dancing around, and they're hitting whack-a-mole moles on the beat. And everything that they do in this video is so deeply uncool that you know that they must really like and trust each other. And their total commitment to what they're doing actually flips the dorkiness and makes it cool.
<v Ira Glass>随着视频继续，他的员工里的青少年也加入了。他们围着跳舞，随着节奏拍打着地鼠。视频里他们所做的一切都非常不酷，这让你知道他们肯定非常喜欢并信任彼此。他们对所做之事的全力投入实际上消解了书呆子气，反而让它变得很酷。

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:29.260
<v Cole Lindbergh>(RAPPING) Get it in the can. Get this ball right in that can. You can do it, man. Just get this ball right in that can, because all I want to do is--
<v Cole Lindbergh>（饶舌）把它投进罐子里。把球投进那个罐子里。你能做到的，伙计。把球投进那个罐子里，因为我只想……

