00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:39.240
<v Cole Lindbergh>(RAPPING) Come play my games.
<v Cole Lindbergh>（饶舌）来玩我的游戏。

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:39.500
<v Cole Lindbergh>[MUSIC - "PAPER PLANES" BY MIA]
<v Cole Lindbergh>（音乐 - M.I.A.的《Paper Planes》）

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:39.760
<v Cole Lindbergh>(RAPPING) All I wanna--
<v Cole Lindbergh>（饶舌）我只想……

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:57.990
<v Ira Glass>There are over a dozen videos, all set in the amusement park, with the stuffed animal prizes always playing surprisingly central roles, like the sci-fi special effects movie they made where a mysterious ray from outer space hits, and the stuffed animal prizes all come to life, seeking vengeance. Key line?
<v Ira Glass>视频有十几部，背景都在游乐园，毛绒玩具奖品总是扮演令人惊讶的核心角色，比如他们制作的那部科幻特效片，一颗来自外太空的神秘射线击中这里，毛绒奖品全部活了过来，寻求复仇。关键台词？

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:04.960
<v Woman>The prizes attacked me. I was in my game. The earth shook. And next thing I knew, I was being pummelled by bears!
<v Woman>奖品攻击了我。我当时在游戏里。大地在震动。接着我就发现自己被熊群痛扁！

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:12.670
<v Ira Glass>The only semi-normal video of the bunch is a training video. This one opens on Cole. He's in a suit and tie in front of a bookcase, reading a book.
<v Ira Glass>这堆视频里唯一半正常的是一个培训视频。这个视频以科尔开场。他穿着西装打着领带，站在书柜前读书。

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:13.330
<v Ira Glass>[FORMAL ORCHESTRAL MUSIC PLAYING]
<v Ira Glass>（正式管弦乐响起）

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:16.480
<v Ira Glass>He looks up, startled, as if the camera surprised him.
<v Ira Glass>他惊讶地抬起头，好像摄像头吓了他一跳。

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:33.610
<v Cole Lindbergh>Hello. How are you? I was just reading. Welcome to the World of Fun Games Training Video. My name is Cole. I'll be taking you on this wonderful journey. Here.
<v Cole Lindbergh>你好。你好吗？我刚才在读书。欢迎观看“欢乐世界”游戏培训视频。我的名字叫科尔。我将带你踏上这段美妙的旅程。来。

00:13:33.610 --> 00:14:02.690
<v Ira Glass>When he says "wonderful journey," he mugs at the camera with this gesture that communicates the idea "I know this is completely ridiculous." In fact, the entire video seems to be making fun of the idea of training videos while, at the same time, it is a training video, explaining how to sign in, how to use the till card, how to stock prizes. I saw these videos, and all I could think of was, these people really love their jobs. And I thought about Michael Scott, the fictional boss on The Office.
<v Ira Glass>当他说“美妙的旅程”时，他对着镜头做了个鬼脸，传达出“我知道这完全荒谬”的意思。事实上，整个视频似乎在嘲笑培训视频这个概念，与此同时，它又确实是一个解释如何签到、如何使用收银机、如何补货奖品的培训视频。我看了这些视频，想到的全是，这些人真的非常热爱他们的工作。我联想到了迈克尔·斯科特，电视剧《办公室》里的虚构老板。

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:33.120
<v Cole Lindbergh>I'd say that there's a lot of Michael Scott in this job. I'd say there's a lot of Michael Scott in me, probably. I do silly things that everybody looks at me later and go, why did he do that? Why was it deemed necessary for Cole to dress up wearing a big beard and a raincoat, and tell everyone he lived downtown under the bridge and he was there to motivational speaker them today? (GRAVELLY VOICE) "Hi, everybody. I'm Phil Bridges"-- and go out and talk to people. What went through his thought process?
<v Cole Lindbergh>我会说这份工作里有很多迈克尔·斯科特的影子。我想我也很有迈克尔·斯科特的成分。我做一些傻事，过后每个人看着我都会问，他为什么那么做？为什么科尔打扮成戴着大胡子、穿着雨衣的样子，告诉大家他住在市中心桥下，他是来给他们做励志演讲的是必须的？（粗糙的声音）“嗨，大家好。我是菲尔·布里奇斯”——然后出去和人交谈。他的心路历程是什么？

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:50.150
<v Cole Lindbergh>And I've run out with a squirt gun all the time. I got my big Super Soaker. And on busy days, I'll take the Super Soaker, and I'll fill it up with ice water, and I'll sneak around the corner and just-- they're all standing there, and I'll just go, "light them up!" and just spray across the whole group.
<v Cole Lindbergh>我经常带着水枪跑出来。我有我的大水枪。在忙碌的日子里，我会带上大水枪，装满冰水，然后潜伏在拐角，等他们都站在那儿，我就喊：“干掉他们！”然后朝整群人喷过去。

00:14:50.150 --> 00:15:20.550
<v Cole Lindbergh>That's what makes it fun! They're going to remember Phil Bridges more than anything else throughout the day. And so if they're talking about, "Did you guys see what Cole did at the shift meeting?" even if they say "that was stupid" or "that was not funny," they're still going to be talking about it. And that's still going to get them happy about this job.
<v Cole Lindbergh>这才是乐趣所在！比起其他任何事，他们会更记得菲尔·布里奇斯。所以如果他们在谈论，“你们看到科尔在晨会上干了什么吗？”，即使他们说“那很蠢”或“一点都不好笑”，他们也还是会谈论它。而这依然能让他们对这份工作感到开心。

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:36.690
<v Ira Glass>So does that work in practice? After all, if you think about it, amusement park jobs are not, on their face, very fun, you know? Taking tickets, strapping people into rides, convincing passersby to throw three balls into a can.
<v Ira Glass>那这在实践中有效吗？毕竟，如果你仔细想想，游乐园的工作表面上其实并不怎么有趣，对吧？检票，给游乐设施上的乘客扣安全带，说服路人把三个球投进罐子里。

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:57.190
<v Ira Glass>Well, the Saturday that I visited turned out to be one of the busiest, hottest days of the summer. There was a concert at the park, which brought in thousands of extra people. And of course, this was Sweet 16 round two, which did seem to matter to the kids. Before the shift, Haley and a couple of the other kids from Games III pulled Cole aside and crowded close so kids from other teams couldn't see.
<v Ira Glass>嗯，我去访的那天碰巧是夏天最忙、最热的日子之一。公园里有场演唱会，带进了成千上万的额外游客。当然，这是“甜蜜16强”第二轮，这对孩子们来说确实很重要。轮班前，海莉和“游戏III”组的其他几个孩子把科尔拉到一边，挤在一起，好让其他组的孩子看不到。

00:15:57.190 --> 00:16:00.350
<v Cole Lindbergh>So this is-- you have a secret weapon that is going--
<v Cole Lindbergh>所以这是……你有一个秘密武器……

